AS-2-TOGGLE-VALIDATOR-001** (open, filed 2026-05-13 from 024B-extras-2 R4 SB-R4-nit-001 / R3 SB-R3-001): `TOP_LEVEL_TOGGLE_KEYS` handler in `validate_restore_source_json()` silently drops fields with non-conforming shape (e.g. an unexpected `{enabled, url, foo}` keyset). The Python validator does NOT check toggle-field shapes — future GitHub API drift introducing a new toggle field with extra metadata would silently omit the field from PUT body with no operator error. Closure: extend the Python validator to assert each `TOP_LEVEL_TOGGLE_KEYS` field is either `bool` or a `dict` with `set(value.keys()) <= {\"enabled\", \"url\"}` (matching the handler's accept set); raise on mismatch. Defensive hardening; not a security bypass (drop-on-mismatch is fail-safe). Owner: future 024B-extras-3 slice OR opportunistic at next ADOPT-001-related work. Does NOT gate 024C.\n361:- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-WORKFLOW-PIN-BASE-BRANCH-001** (open): `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml` invokes `scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh` from the PR's checked-out code (PR HEAD), not the base branch. For future multi-operator adoption, pin enforcement to `git show origin/main:scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh | bash -s -- ...` or use a reusable workflow from base. Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice (depth-defense); does NOT gate 024C.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
