onical`, `restore-checks-wrong-context-ack`, and `restore-log-sanitization` during this fix-round. Surfaced by step-7 demo + R22 + R25 against real GitHub API (the 3rd mock-masking CRIT in this slice's history). Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice; does NOT gate 024C.\n- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-TOGGLE-VALIDATOR-001** (open, filed 2026-05-13 from 024B-extras-2 R4 SB-R4-nit-001 / R3 SB-R3-001): `TOP_LEVEL_TOGGLE_KEYS` handler in `validate_restore_source_json()` silently drops fields with non-conforming shape (e.g. an unexpected `{enabled, url, foo}` keyset). The Python validator does NOT check toggle-field shapes — future GitHub API drift introducing a new toggle field with extra metadata would silently omit the field from PUT body with no operator error. Closure: extend the Python validator to assert each `TOP_LEVEL_TOGGLE_KEYS` field is either `bool` or a `dict` with `set(value.keys()) <= {\"enabled\", \"url\"}` (matching the handler's accept set); raise on mismatch. Defensive hardening; not a security bypass (drop-on-mismatch is fail-safe). Owner: future 024B-extras-3 slice OR opportunistic at next ADOPT-001-related work. Does NOT gate 024C.\n- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-TRANSFORM-INCLUSION-LIST-001** (closed 2026-05-13: implemented in 024B-extras-2 per D-048): `validate_restore_source_json()` `transform()` uses an exclusion-list approach — unknown GitHub branch-protection fields pass through to the PUT body. R30 surfaced `lock_branch`, `required_linear_history`, `block_creations` (and any future similar) pass through with NO posture-degradation guard, allowing a malicious pre-state to enable these without operator ack. Closure: switch to inclusion-list transform (explicitly allowed fields) + posture-degradation acknowledgement flags for each guarded sub-field. Aligns with the depth-defense surface carve (SCOPE-CORRECTION-2-2026-05-11.md). Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice (D-048); does NOT gate 024C — current exclusion list is sufficient for cohort onboarding under invariant 7's <30-min SLO since cohort pre-states are operator-captured from REAL adopter GET (not attacker-crafted).\n- **TF-024B-STEP7-DEMO-001** (closed 2026-05-11): --restore real-repo round-trip evidence at `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/restore-roundtrip-evidence.md` — operator-interactive demo at dispatch-plan step 7 completed against `jrnb2024/scp-024b-extras-restore-test` throw-away repo. **Surfaced CRIT** (mock-masking: transform did not unwrap `*.enabled` sub-objects for `required_linear_history`/`allow_force_pushes`/etc → HTTP 422 on real PUT); closed in fix-round-22 with generic `{enabled: bool}` unwrap + PUT-body-shape assertion test. Round-trip succeeded post-fix; all 4 key fields matched state-A target. Throw-away repo cleanup deferred — current gh token lacks `delete_repo` scope.\n- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-RESTORE-PATH-CONTAINMENT-001** (closed 2026-05-13: implemented in 024B-extras-2 per D-048): apply `resolve_inside_repo_root()` guard to `scripts/enable-required-check.sh --restore <path>` argument in 024B-extras-2 alongside other defensive hardening. Low blast-radius (operator-credentials-bound). Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice; does NOT gate 024C.\n- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-COHORT-REGEX-MULTICHAR-001** (open): widen `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml` cohort regex from `024[C-F]/` to `024[C-F][^/]*/` for future multi-char cohort slice IDs. Current 5-cohort set (024C/D/E/F) is single-char and unaffected; defensive. Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice; does NOT gate 024C.\n- **TF-024B-STEP7-FIXTURE-SEQ-001** (open): align DISPATCH-NOTE step-7 fixture sequence with `restore-roundtrip-evidence-PLACEHOLDER.md` (add or harmonise `Mutate branch protection` step description). Will be resolved naturally at step-7 demo execution time.\n- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-STAGED-RESTORE-TEST-001** (closed 2026-05-13: implemented in 024B-extras-2 per D-048): add test case for staged-but-uncommitted prior-restore evidence in 024B-extras-2 tests (guards against future narrowing of `git diff HEAD` to `git